      {
       "uuid": "7e5564f4-814c-4d8d-9f95-c22a159d187c",
       "reviewer_name": "Anonymous",
       "reviewer_initial": "A",
       "title": "False advertisement",
       "body_html": "<p>This website is advertising a 45 day money back guarantee. Verbatim “ 45 Day Money-Back\n<br />Guarantee\n<br />We're confident this is the best vitamin you'll ever try. But we understand you may be skeptical. So give it a try...worry-free! If you're still not happy, just send it back.” I contacted to send them back and they said-  “ Unfortunately, due to food safety regulations, we’re unable to accept returns or issue refunds once an order has shipped. I truly apologize for any inconvenience this may cause.</p>\n\n<p>However, we can offer a store credit for the amount, which you can use toward a future purchase, or a one-time swap for a different variant” I told them I would leave this information in my review and gather my refund w my CC company behind me. You cannot advertise something and not follow through. They’ve lost any future business from me and hopefully this deters your purchase.</p>",
